.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH RIAKCTL 1 "2026-11-02" "libriak-c @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
riakctl \- command-line client for Riak KV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B riakctl
.RI [ "global options" ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B riakctl
reaches Riak KV nodes over the network, through Protocol Buffers or HTTP,
with TLS and Riak security, and makes their data and operational
interfaces available to shell scripts: objects, listings, secondary
indexes, the Query API, MapReduce, data types, bucket properties, Riak
Search, AAE folds, nextgenrepl queues, statistics, and backups
and restores. It is built on libriak-c and works with Riak KV 2.0 to 3.4.
.PP
Results are printed as JSON; listings, folds and streams as JSON Lines
(one value per line), suited to
.BR jq (1).
Single JSON documents are indented when standard output is a terminal.
Errors are reported on standard error and through the exit status.
.PP
Node operations (cluster membership changes, bucket type creation,
security users and grants, transfers) are not available remotely in Riak;
they remain with
.BR "riak admin" .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Environment variables are given in brackets; options take precedence.
.TP
.BI "\-u, \-\-url " URLS
Nodes, as
.BR pb:// ,
.B pbs://
(Protocol Buffers with STARTTLS),
.B http://
or
.B https://
.IR host [: port ]
entries separated by commas; all entries share one scheme and IPv6
addresses are written in brackets [RIAK_URL]. Default:
.BR pb://127.0.0.1:8087 .
.TP
.BI \-\-http\-port " PORT"
HTTP port used for statistics and the Query API over Protocol Buffers
[RIAK_HTTP_PORT]; default 8098 for pb://, none for pbs://.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
Riak security user [RIAK_USER]; needs pbs:// or https://.
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " FILE"
File whose first line is the password. RIAK_PASSWORD holds the password
itself. Passwords are not accepted on the command line.
.TP
.BI \-\-ca " FILE"
CA bundle (PEM) for certificate verification [RIAK_CA].
.TP
.BI \-\-cert " FILE" ", \-\-key " FILE
Client certificate and key (PEM) [RIAK_CERT, RIAK_KEY].
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
The server certificate is not verified.
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-legacy
Interoperability with the TLS stack of Riak 2.x [RIAK_TLS_LEGACY=1].
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " MS" ", \-\-connect\-timeout " MS
Whole-request timeout (default none) and connection timeout (default 5000).
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Additional attempts after a failure (default 2).
.TP
.BI "\-t, \-\-type " TYPE
Bucket type for the commands that take one; also accepted after the
command name.
.TP
.BR \-\-pretty ", " \-\-compact
Indented or single-line JSON documents.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Client log on standard error.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
.SH COMMANDS
.B riakctl help
.I command
describes the options of each command.
.TP
.BR ping " [" \-\-all ]
Pings every node; fails unless one (with \-\-all: every one) answers.
.TP
.B info
Node name and version, client node health, cluster members.
.TP
.BR stats " [" \fINAME\fR | \fIPREFIX\fB*\fR ...]
Node statistics, optionally only the named entries.
.TP
.BI get " BUCKET KEY"
The value as stored; \-\-json for the object with its metadata, \-\-all for
every sibling, \-\-head for the metadata only.
.TP
.BI put " BUCKET " \fR[\fIKEY\fR]
Stores standard input, \-\-value or \-\-file, with \-\-content\-type,
\-\-meta, \-\-index, \-\-link, \-\-vclock and \-\-create; without a key one is
generated.
.TP
.BI delete " BUCKET KEY"
.TP
.BR list " buckets | keys " \fIBUCKET
Bucket or key listing (expensive), \-\-plain for plain lines.
.TP
.BI backup " BUCKET"
Writes the bucket to standard output or \-o FILE; see BACKUPS.
.TP
.BR restore " [" \-j\~\fIN\fR "] [" \fIFILE\fR]
Restores a backup with N worker threads (default 4); see BACKUPS.
.TP
.BI index " BUCKET INDEX VALUE" "\fR | \fP" "BUCKET INDEX MIN MAX"
Secondary index query; streamed, or one page with \-\-max and
\-\-continuation.
.TP
.BI query " BUCKET INDEX"
Query API request (Riak 3.4+) from flags or \-\-request FILE.
.TP
.BR mapred " [" \-\-collect "] [" \fIFILE\fR]
MapReduce job; phase results streamed, or collected.
.TP
.BI coverage " BUCKET" "\fR, \fPpreflist" " BUCKET KEY"
Coverage plan and preference list (Protocol Buffers).
.TP
.BI "dt get" "\fR|\fPincr\fR|\fPdecr\fR|\fPadd\fR|\fPremove\fR|\fPupdate ..."
Data types in a bucket type with a datatype property.
.TP
.BI "counter get" "\fR|\fPincr\fR|\fPdecr BUCKET KEY \fR[\fIN\fR]"
Riak 1.4 counters.
.TP
.BI "props get" "\fR|\fPset\fR|\fPreset BUCKET\fR, \fPprops type\-get" "\fR|\fPtype\-set TYPE"
Bucket and bucket type properties.
.TP
.B search query\fR|\fPindex\-list\fR|\fPindex\-get\fR|\fPindex\-create\fR|\fPindex\-delete\fR|\fPschema\-get\fR|\fPschema\-put
Riak Search (Riak 2.x).
.TP
.B aae root\fR|\fPbranches\fR|\fPclocks\fR|\fPbuckets\fR|\fPtree\fR|\fPkeys\fR|\fPfind\fR|\fPstats\fR|\fPtombs\fR|\fPreap\fR|\fPerase\fR|\fPrepair\fR|\fPrepl\fR|\fPcompare
AAE folds (Riak 2.9+ with tictac AAE). Reap and erase only count unless
\-\-local or \-\-job is given. compare lists the keys whose vector clocks
differ between two clusters (\-\-peer URL, by comparing trees) or two
buckets (\-\-peer\-bucket, key by key, in ranges of at most
\-\-chunk keys per side paged from the $bucket index).
.TP
.B repl fetch\fR|\fPpush\fR|\fPmembers\fR|\fPcluster\-id\fR|\fPget
nextgenrepl queues and riak_repl.
.SH BACKUPS
A backup is a JSON Lines file: a header
.RB ( {"format":"riakctl\-backup","version":1,...} ),
one line per key with its vector clock and every sibling (value, content
type, metadata, secondary indexes, links, last-modified time), or with
the value of a data type, and a trailer
.RB ( {"end":true,"count": N } ).
A file without the trailer is incomplete, and restore reports it.
Tombstones are not saved. Keys are enumerated by an object fold, an AAE
clock fold or a key listing
.RB ( \-\-method ),
the first available being used by default.
.PP
A restore is idempotent: keys that already hold every sibling of the
backup are left alone. A single sibling is written "as is", keeping the
backed-up vector clock; Riak then keeps a newer version already stored,
as replication does. Several siblings are written one by one and become
siblings again in allow_mult buckets; in a bucket without allow_mult only
the last modified sibling is written (reported as collapsed). Counters are restored through the
difference to the stored value, sets by adding elements, maps field by
field; HyperLogLogs cannot be restored. Entries longer than
\-\-max\-line bytes (default 256 MiB) are skipped and counted as failed.
.PP
Keys and bucket names are C strings in libriak-c: names that contain a
NUL byte are left out of listings, folds and AAE results. riakctl then
warns, adds
.B left_out
to the trailer of a backup and exits with status 1.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
other error (server error, malformed response, failed restore entries)
.TP
.B 2
usage error or invalid configuration
.TP
.B 3
not found
.TP
.B 4
the object has siblings (get \-\-all shows them)
.TP
.B 5
precondition failed (put \-\-create on an existing key)
.TP
.B 6
authentication or permission failure
.TP
.B 7
no node reachable (connection, DNS, timeout or TLS failure)
.TP
.B 8
not supported by the node's Riak version or by the transport
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
riakctl \-u pbs://riak1:8087,pbs://riak2:8087 \-\-user ops \e
        \-\-password\-file ~/.riak\-pass \-\-ca ca.pem ping
echo '{"name":"alice"}' | riakctl put \-c application/json \e
        \-i email_bin=alice@example.com users alice
riakctl index users email_bin a z \-\-terms | jq \-r .key
riakctl backup \-o users.jsonl users && riakctl restore users.jsonl
riakctl aae keys users | riakctl repl push q1
echo '{"visits_counter":1}' | riakctl \-t maps dt update profiles alice
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jq (1),
.BR riak (1).
The libriak-c documentation, docs/riakctl.md, and the demo scripts in
examples/cli describe the commands and workflows in detail.
